---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import CarePreview from '../../components/CarePreview.astro';
import { carecontextGithub, carecontextGithubLabel } from '../../data/projects.mjs';
const root = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Base title="CareContext — Harikrishna Trivedi" description="A research prototype for PubMed literature discovery and evidence review over fictional records.">
  <section class="case-hero shell"><a href={`${root}#work`} class="back-link">← Back to selected work</a><div class="case-category">HEALTHTECH / EVIDENCE EXPLORATION / 2026</div><h1>CareContext<span>.</span></h1><p class="case-deck">Keep the source.<br/><em>Keep the context.</em></p><div class="case-actions"><a class="primary-link" href={carecontextGithub} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{carecontextGithubLabel} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="case-facts"><div><span>PROJECT</span><p>Independent portfolio project</p></div><div><span>MY FOCUS</span><p>Product scope, implementation & evaluation</p></div><div><span>STACK</span><p>Python · FastAPI · SQLite · JavaScript</p></div><div><span>STATUS</span><p>Research prototype · v0.2</p></div></div></section>
  <div class="shell" data-reveal><figure class="project-stage case-main-stage care-stage"><div class="stage-corner">SOURCES FIRST. CONTEXT ALWAYS.</div><CarePreview/><figcaption>Interface illustration, not an application screenshot</figcaption></figure></div>
  <section class="case-section shell"><div class="case-section-label">01 / THE QUESTION</div><div class="case-copy" data-reveal><h2>What if inspecting the evidence<br/>felt like part of the answer?</h2><p>CareContext explores two related workflows: discovering public medical literature, and reviewing a small collection of fictional records with dated source excerpts. The common thread is provenance: keeping what was found attached to where it came from.</p><p>The literature workspace searches PubMed and exposes study metadata, abstracts, and outbound source links. The record workspace uses synthetic examples to explore retrieval, citations, evidence gaps, and reviewer notes.</p></div></section>
  <section class="case-chapters shell"><div class="section-topline"><span class="section-index">02 / THE EXPERIENCE</span><span class="section-aside">Three decisions that shape the product.</span></div><div class="case-chapter-grid"><article data-reveal><span class="chapter-number">01</span><h3>Start with a question.</h3><p>Search literature with study-type and year filters. Show the query so the retrieval process remains visible.</p><div class="mini-query">A research question <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div></article><article data-reveal><span class="chapter-number">02</span><h3>Open the source.</h3><p>Inspect the abstract and metadata, or follow the PubMed and DOI links to read further.</p><div class="mini-source"><i aria-hidden="true">↗</i><span>Title · Publication · Year<br/><strong>Source stays attached.</strong></span></div></article><article data-reveal><span class="chapter-number">03</span><h3>Keep uncertainty visible.</h3><p>In synthetic record review, preserve dated excerpts and show evidence gaps rather than filling them with plausible prose.</p><div class="mini-evidence"><span aria-hidden="true">[1]</span> An inspectable source excerpt</div></article></div></section>
  <section class="case-section shell"><div class="case-section-label">03 / ENGINEERING NOTES</div><div class="case-copy" data-reveal><h2>Useful boundaries<br/>are part of the design.</h2><div class="engineering-row"><h3>Two distinct evidence paths</h3><p>Live literature retrieval uses PubMed E-utilities. Synthetic record retrieval uses a local, case-scoped BM25 baseline. Their results stay separate.</p></div><div class="engineering-row"><h3>Source verification has a specific job</h3><p>The record workspace checks that excerpts match the supplied source passages. That verifies provenance within the fixture collection; it does not establish clinical truth.</p></div><div class="engineering-row"><h3>A deliberate prototype boundary</h3><p>No real patient data, diagnosis, treatment recommendations, EHR integration, or clinical validation. The literature workspace discovers sources; it does not generate a clinical answer.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="case-reflection shell" data-reveal><span class="section-index">04 / HOW IT WAS BUILT</span><h2>AI accelerated the work.<br/><span>Review gave it direction.</span></h2><p>I used AI assistance for implementation and documentation, with explicit scope, source checks, and evaluation fixtures. The project is an exploration of evidence-aware software, and its limitations remain part of the presentation.</p><div class="case-actions"><a href={carecontextGithub} class="primary-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{carecontextGithubLabel} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href={`${root}work/patchpilot/`} class="primary-link">Next: PatchPilot AI <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></section>
</Base>
